---
import Doc from '../../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import Pager from '../../../components/Pager.astro';
const slug = 'getting-started/install';
---
<Doc slug={slug} title="Install">
  <h1>Install</h1>
  <p class="lede">Get the cortex binary on your machine in one of three ways.</p>

  <h2>go install</h2>
  <p>If you have a Go toolchain, this is the fastest path:</p>
  <pre><code>go install github.com/atakang7/cortex/cmd/cortex@latest</code></pre>
  <p>The binary lands in your <code>$GOPATH/bin</code> — make sure that's on your <code>$PATH</code>.</p>

  <h2>Pre-built binaries</h2>
  <p>
    Every <a href="https://github.com/atakang7/cortex/releases">release</a> ships binaries for
    <code>linux</code> and <code>darwin</code> on <code>amd64</code> and <code>arm64</code>.
    Download the archive for your platform, extract it, and put the <code>cortex</code>
    binary somewhere on your <code>$PATH</code>.
  </p>
  <pre><code>curl -L https://github.com/atakang7/cortex/releases/latest/download/cortex-linux-amd64.tar.gz \
  | tar xz -C /usr/local/bin cortex</code></pre>

  <h2>Build from source</h2>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/atakang7/cortex.git
cd cortex
go build -o cortex ./cmd/cortex</code></pre>

  <h2>Verify</h2>
  <p>Check that it runs and prints build metadata:</p>
  <pre><code>cortex --version</code></pre>
  <pre><code>cortex 1.2.3 (abc1234, built 2025-01-01T00:00:00Z)</code></pre>

  <div class="callout info">
    <span class="ico">ℹ️</span>
    <div class="callout-body">
      <strong>What's next?</strong> cortex needs a model before it can start. Continue to
      <a href="/cortex/docs/getting-started/quick-start/">Quick start</a> to configure one.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="docs-pager"><Pager slug={slug} /></div>
</Doc>
